setBackgroundColorColumn [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Sets the background color of the specified column(s) of the TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.setBackgroundColorColumn(Column:any [,Column:any,...], 
BackgroundColor:integer)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Column of data type any designates the column whose background color you want to
set.
• The optional parameters Column of data type any designate additional columns whose background
color you want to set.
• The parameter BackgroundColor of data type integer designates the color.
You can specify 1 for Black, 2 for Red, 3 for Green, 4 for Blue, 5 for Magenta, 6 for Yellow or 7 for
Cyan.
Set the RGB values of the color with the method makeRGBValue.
Example
timeSequence1.setBackgroundColorColumn(1,1) 
// sets the background color of column 1 to black
timeSequence1.setBackgroundColorColumn(1,2,2) 
// sets the background color of columns 1 and 2 to red
