setBackgroundColorRow [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Sets the background color of the specified row(s) of the TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.setBackgroundColorRow(Row:any[, Row:any,...], 
BackgroundColor:integer)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Row of data type any designates the row whose background color you want to set.
• The optional parameters Row of data type any designate additional rows whose background color you
want to set.
• The parameter BackgroundColor of data type integer designates the background color.
You can specify 1 for Black, 2 for Red, 3 for Green, 4 for Blue, 5 for Magenta, 6 for Yellow, or 7 for
Cyan.
Set the RGB values of the color with the method makeRGBValue.
Examples
var rgb: integer
// sets the background color of row 3
MyTimeSequence.setBackgroundColorRow(3,makeRGBValue(0,200,0))
// sets the background color of rows 4 and 8
MyTimeSequence.setBackgroundColorRow(4,8,makeRGBValue(60,100,0))
print MyTimeSequence.getBackgroundColorRow(3)
// sets the background color of row 1 to black
MyTimeSequence.setBackgroundColorRow(1,1) 
// sets the background color of rows 1 and 2 to red
MyTimeSequence.setBackgroundColorRow(1,2,2) 
