[ , ] [SimTalk] - read cell contents, TimeSequence
The TimeSequence designated by <Path> enables you to randomly access the contents of the cells by
employing the column and row indexes.
Remarks
The index statement begins and ends with a bracket. Within the bracket you first enter the column and
then the row of the cell to be accessed. The data type of the return value is the same as the data type of
the table cell. Plant Simulation just reads the contents of the cell but does not remove it!
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>[Column:integer, Row:integer] → contents of the cell
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Column of data type integer designates the column.
• The parameter Row of data type integer designates the row.
Return Value
The return value is the contents of the cell.
Is VOID if the cell is empty.
Example
print timeSequence[1,2]
print timeSequence["Value",2]
[ , ] [SimTalk] - read cell contents, TimeSequence
11-4310 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

[ , ] [SimTalk] - write cell contents, TimeSequence
Writes data to the specified cell of the TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>[Column:integer, Row:integer]
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Column of data type integer designates the column.
• The parameter Row of data type integer designates the row.
First you access the cell by its index and then you assign a value.
The index statement starts and ends with a bracket. In the bracket you first enter the column and then the
row of the cell to be accessed. The data type of the new value has to be the same as the data type of the
table cell.
Example
timeSequence[2,3] := 12.34
[ , ] [SimTalk] - write cell contents, TimeSequence
Plant Simulation Help 11-4311
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

add [SimTalk]
Either adds a numerical value to all entries of the value column of the TimeSequence designated by <Path>
or combines the time and value columns of two TimeSequence objects.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.add(ValueToBeAdded:any)
Parameter
If the parameter ValueToBeAdded of data type any which is to be added is a numerical value, Plant
Simulation adds it to each entry of the value column. The time column remains unchanged.
If the parameter ValueToBeAdded is another TimeSequence, Plant Simulation adds time value pairs in
sections. The values in the time columns determine the extent of the individual sections. If for a certain
time value there are multiple entries in one time sequence, and only one entry in the other time sequence,
the single entry will be added to all other entries. If both time sequences have the same number of
multiple entries with a particular time value, the entries will be combined in pairs and added afterwards.
If the number of entries with the same time value differs, the last entry will be duplicated, before the
addition is performed, until the number of entries with the same time matches.
Example
MyTimeSequence.add(5)
shiftA.add(shiftB)
add [SimTalk]
11-4312 Plant Simulation Help
