and [SimTalk] - operator
You can use boolean operations, such as and and or, in a TimeSequence of data type boolean.
Remarks
The boolean operation may be executed with a single boolean parameter or another TimeSequence
object. In the latter case, the sequence of values in the time column will be the union of the time columns
of both time sequences involved in the operation.
Type
Method/operator
Syntax
<Path>.and(Operand:any)
Parameter
The parameter Operand of data type any designates the operand which will be applied.
Example
failureA.and(failureB)
workerA.or(workerB)
MyTimeSequence.or(true)
MyTimeSequence.and(false)
See also
or [SimTalk] - operator
and [SimTalk] - operator
Plant Simulation Help 11-4313
