divide [SimTalk]
Divides all items of the value column of the TimeSequence designated by <Path> by a numerical value.
Remarks
In addition, a time sequence may be divided by another time sequence. Then, the time column of the
result is the combination of the time column of both time sequences. The value column of the result
contains the quotient of the values of both time sequences at the respective times.
Note
All divisors must be non-zero.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.divide(Divisor:any)
Parameter
The parameter Divisor of data type any designates the divisor which will be applied.
Example
MyTimeSequence.divide(5)
numEntities.divide(current.NumMU)
divide [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4315
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

include [SimTalk]
Takes all entries of the TimeSequence designated by the parameter of data type object and inserts them in
the TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Inserting all entries may result in a single time sequence containing multiple entries with the same time
value. If this happens, the order of the entries with identical time values, with respect to each other, is
undefined.
The data types of the affected time sequences must be identical or compatible.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.include(TimeSequence:object)
Parameter
The parameter TimeSequence of data type object designates the TimeSequence whose values will be
included.
Example
timeSequence1.include(timeSequence2)
include [SimTalk]
11-4316 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

insert [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Inserts a time/value pair into the TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.insert(GivenTime:any, Value:any)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter GivenTime of data type any designates the time.
For the time reference Absolute, this parameter is expected to be of data type dateTime. Otherwise, the
data type time is required.
• The parameter Value of data type any designates the value.
The type of the value for this parameter, must match or be compatible with the data type of the
TimeSequence.
Example
MyTimeSequence.insert(eventcontroller.simtime,3)
MyTimeSequence.insert(sysdate,3)
insert [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
