repeat [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Deletes all entries of the TimeSequence designated by <Path> and replaces them with copies of a sub-
range of the data of another TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.repeat(TimeSequence:object, Subrange:time, NumberOfCopies:real)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter TimeSequence of data type object designates the TimeSequence whose subrange will be
pasted.
• The parameter Subrange of data type time designates the sub-range. It starts with the time zero and
ends at the time designated by this parameter.
• The parameter NumberOfCopies of data type real designates the number of copies of the data which are
to be inserted.
You might, for example, use this to create a week’s schedule from a day’s schedule by repeating it five
times.
Example
LengthOfDay := str_to_time("1:00:00:00.00")
weekPlan.repeat(dayPlan,lengthOfDay,5)
repeat [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Plant Simulation Help 11-4321
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

repeatTo [SimTalk]
Removes all entries of the TimeSequence designated by <Path> and replaces them with copies of a
sub-range of the data of the designated TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.repeatTo(TimeSequence:object, Subrange:time, RangeToBeFilled:time)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter TimeSequence of data type object designates the TimeSequence whose data will replace
the existing data.
• The parameter Subrange of data type time designates the sub-range. It starts with the time zero and
ends at the time designated by this parameter.
• The parameter RangeToBeFilled of data type time designates the range of the TimeSequence designated
by <Path> that is to be filled with copies of the sub-range.
Consequently, the range of the TimeSequence designated by <Path> must be greater than the sub-
range of the TimeSequence designated by the parameter of data type object. Otherwise, it would
remain empty.
Examples
weekPeriod := str_to_time("5:00:00:00.00")
dayPeriod := str_to_time("1:00:00:00.00")
weekPlan.repeatTo(dayPlan,weekPeriod,dayPeriod)
MyTimeSequence.or(true) // all values := true
MyTimeSequence.and(false) // all values := false
repeatTo [SimTalk]
11-4322 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

subtract [SimTalk]
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.subtract(ValueToBeSubtracted:integer)
<Path>.subtract(ValueToBeSubtracted:real)
<Path>.subtract(ValueToBeSubtracted:object)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• If the parameter to subtract is a numerical value designated by the parameter ValueToBeSubtracted of
data type integer or real, Plant Simulation subtracts it from each entry of the value column. The time
column remains unchanged.
• If the parameter to subtract is another TimeSequence designated by the parameter
ValueToBeSubtracted of data type object, Plant Simulation subtracts time value pairs in sections. The
values in the time columns set the extent of the individual sections. If for a certain time value there are
multiple entries in one time sequence, and only one entry in the other time sequence, the single entry
will be subtracted from all other entries.
If both TimeSequences contain the same number of multiple entries with a particular time value, Plant
Simulation combines the entries in pairs and subtracts them afterwards. If the number of entries with
the same time value differs, Plant Simulation duplicates the last entry, before it subtracts it, until the
number of entries with the same time matches.
Example
MyTimeSequence.subtract(5)
stock.subtract(missingEntities)
subtract [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4323
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

value [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Returns the value the TimeSequence designated by <Path> taken at a given time.
Remarks
If there are multiple entries with the same time, Plant Simulation returns the entry with the highest
number.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.value(GivenTime:time) -> any
Parameter
The parameter GivenTime of data type time designates the column.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
Example
print ts1.value(1.5)+ts2.value(1.5)
Read-Only Attributes of the TimeSequence
Read-Only Attributes of the TimeSequence
The TimeSequence provides:
• The _Read-Only Attributes of Lists and Tables.
• The _Read-Only Attributes of All Objects.
You can query the values of the read-only attributes, but you cannot set them as Plant Simulation
computes the value for the point-in-time at which you query it. In most cases a read-only attribute
corresponds to an unavailable dialog item on one of the tabs of the object, for example on the tab
Statistics.
value [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
